  ==> At y=1 fixed, even at x=0 exactly, y*R(y)=0.6556795424, NOT close to 1.
      The quantity does NOT saturate toward 1 merely by sending x->0 at fixed,
      moderate y. (Monotonic decrease in x is visible above, consistent with R
      being a decreasing function -- so the SUP over x of y*R(x+y), for fixed y,
      IS attained at x=0, but that value itself is far from 1 unless y is ALSO large.)

G3. Repeat G2 at a LARGE fixed y (y=100) -- does saturation appear only here?
